   "title": "Stitch + SAM mask",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "STITCH + the optional SAM mask\n\nThe two nodes to the left - SAMLoader and H3 Face Mask (SAM) - ship MUTED, and stay\nwired. Unmute both (Ctrl+M) to swap the rect paste mask for a true face-shaped one.\nMuted, this graph needs no SAM model. Unmuted it also needs one, in models/sams/.\nComfyUI-Impact-Pack is required either way: its subpack registers the ultralytics\nmodel folders, and this graph's detector values use that naming.\n\nFEATHER IS IN SOURCE PIXELS, and the two masks want very different values. This graph\nships 24 for the rect. With a SAM mask drop it to 4-8.\n\nKEY POINT: the wide crop exists to give the SAMPLER CONTEXT. It is NOT what gets\npasted. Only the face region composites; everything else keeps its original pixels.\n\nSAM MASKS THE INPUT, NEVER THE OUTPUT. The mask node takes the TRACKER's crops, not\nthe decoded result - the same way FaceDetailer computes its mask from the source\nimage. Mask the generated result instead and, if the model nudges the face inward,\nthe mask traces the NEW smaller silhouette while the original face pokes out past it\n- most visibly the nose on profile shots. It is also cheaper: no dependency on the\nsampler, so SAM need not be resident alongside the video model.\n\nWORTH KNOWING: a rect mask often BEATS SAM. SAM traces the face tightly, so any drift\nin the refined face lands right on the silhouette. A slightly looser rect puts the\nseam in hair and background where it reads far less. That is why it is the default."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
