   "title": "Model / encoder",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "MODEL AND TEXT ENCODER\n\nWired: UNETLoader + CLIPLoader, loading pruned int8 weights and an\nnvfp4 text encoder. This is the combination these examples were\nbuilt and tested against.\n\nMuted beside them: UnetLoaderGGUF + CLIPLoaderGGUF, the GGUF route.\nIt needs the ComfyUI-GGUF pack, which is why it is not the default\nhere - but it is a real alternative and fits in less VRAM.\n\nTo use GGUF instead: mute the two loaders above, un-mute these two,\nand connect UnetLoaderGGUF -> LoraLoaderModelOnly and\nCLIPLoaderGGUF -> MiniMax H3 Reference To Video.\n\nWhatever you load, the turbo LoRA and the step count must agree:\nthe 8-step LoRA wired here wants steps=8 on BasicScheduler. A\n4-step LoRA wants 4. Mismatch them and the result is mush or a\nwaste of time."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 111,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -1860,
    1485
   ],
   "size": [
    330,
    300
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Audio source",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "AUDIO - drives lipsync\n\nWired: the audio track of the source clip, straight off the video\nloader. That is the simple case and needs nothing extra.\n\nMuted beside it: Load Audio (Upload). Un-mute it and wire its\naudio output to BOTH MiniMax H3 Reference To Video and MiniMax H3\nNative Audio Lock, in place of the video's own.\n\nWorth doing when you have an isolated VOCAL stem. H3 shapes the\nmouth from whatever audio it is given, so a full mix - music,\neffects, other voices - is competing with the speech. A vocals-only\ntrack gives cleaner lipsync.\n\nThe audio wired here must cover the same stretch of time as the\nframes being refined, or the mouth will follow the wrong sound."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
